205:**Signal emission is mode-aware.** `PropagationEngine::emit(mode, event)` accepts the mode and routes: in `Live`, it writes to the signal bus and triggers propagation; in `Simulate`/`Evaluate`, it records the event to the tracer and returns without side effect. The engine is not mutated in non-Live modes.
207:**External calls are mode-aware.** Services that call external APIs (Glean, Slack, Gmail, Salesforce) check mode at the call boundary and route to either the live client (`Live`) or a replay fixture supplied by the `EvalFixture` (`Simulate`/`Evaluate`). The replay fixture API is specified in [ADR-0107](0107-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md).
209:**Intelligence provider is mode-aware via injection.** In `Live`, `AbilityContext.intelligence` is the production provider. In `Simulate`/`Evaluate`, it is a replay provider constructed from the `EvalFixture` and matched by prompt hash. The provider interface ([ADR-0091](0091-intelligence-provider-abstraction.md)) is the same; only the implementation differs per mode.
