    56	## 4. Security
    57	
    58	New attack surfaces are schema-driven JSON invocation, actor-filtered introspection, docs output, and macro-enforced metadata. JSON input is deserialized only through the registry wrapper and schema-validated before and after invocation. Actor filtering is enforced in `iter_for` and every invoke path; enumeration does not leak maintenance/admin-only names or schemas to `Actor::Agent`, matching ADR-0102 (`.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:250-258`).
